BFS on a graph is the grid BFS from the BFS lesson with node numbers in place of cells: a `std::queue<int>` and a `dist` vector that starts at -1 for unvisited. The first time BFS reaches a node, it got there by a path with the fewest edges. The new part is a `parent` vector that records who discovered each node, so you can rebuild the path itself.

